  "_comment": "Cross-check fixture for the Kotlin engine and its Python port. Small on purpose, but it exercises the parts that are easy to get subtly wrong: rarity (action is common, espionnage is rare), the per-author cap (kishimoto carries four series), role weighting (a colorist credit must count less than a writer one), a term carried by EVERY series (bd, which the engine skips outright), and book tags. Regenerate the expected file with: python bench.py emit-expected",
